From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] amigavideo: turn on the driver's own tracing

It carries 165 D(bug()) calls -- its author traced every step of mode
setting, the compositor and the bitmap class -- and on this port it hangs
during its own initialisation, with OpenLibrary("amigavideo.hidd")
handing the AmigaVideo task a NULL.

Sampling the m68k PC from outside named two functions and went no
further. Writing another probe would be building what is already here.

Temporary: turn it off again once ISSUE-0081 is closed. It is a great
deal of output on a serial line the rest of the boot has to share.
---
 arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/mmakefile.src | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/mmakefile.src b/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/mmakefile.src
--- a/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/mmakefile.src
+++ b/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/mmakefile.src
@@ -16,6 +16,17 @@
                -D__GRAPHICS_NOLIBBASE__ \
                -D__UTILITY_NOLIBBASE__ \
                -D__GRAPHICS_NOHIDDBASE__
-#USER_CPPFLAGS += -DDEBUG=1
+# Turned ON, deliberately and temporarily.
+#
+# This driver carries 165 D(bug()) calls -- its author traced every step of
+# mode setting, the compositor and the bitmap class -- and on this port it
+# hangs during its own initialisation with OpenLibrary("amigavideo.hidd")
+# handing the AmigaVideo task a NULL. Sampling the m68k PC from outside got as
+# far as naming two functions and no further, and inventing another probe
+# would be building what is already here.
+#
+# Turn it off again once ISSUE-0081 is closed: it is a great deal of output on
+# a serial line that the rest of the boot has to share.
+USER_CPPFLAGS += -DDEBUG=1
 
 OPTIMIZATION_CFLAGS := $(ROM_OPTIMIZATION_CFLAGS)
